<title>UK: HSBC reorganises two U.S. units.</title>
<headline>HSBC reorganises two U.S. units.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hongkong and Shanghai Banking Corporation Ltd said on Wednesday that it had sold businesses worth $27 million in the United States to one of its subsidiaries, a joint venture between HSBC Holdings Plc and Wells Fargo and Co.</p>
<p>The sale comprises two separate transactions, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>In the first transaction Hongkong Bank sold the trade services assets and businesses of its California and Texas branches and in another it sold its assets in its Portland and Seattle offices.</p>
</text>
